{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And Noah began.</b> He began with an unfit deed, and from this there ensued acts that ought not be done — for indeed a small measure of corruption at the start brings about much from it at the end, as happens in the sciences from an error at the outset. This itself is indicated by the verse: וַיָּחֶל הָעָם לִזְנוֹת (Numbers 25:1)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:36.829829083Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}